  "claim_boundary": "This package freezes only a repository-contract-level, zero-output source-opportunity preflight. It distinguishes protocol freeze from source-stage completion; binds the immutable v4a lineage and the existing three-action owner; preallocates a fixed max-N root order; freezes typed blueprint levels, balanced hidden fact orientations, Latin-rotated semantic strata, total utility-vector constraints, and one exact final-32K twin transform; and preregisters an explicit 512-atom generic-decision synthetic nine-arm potential-outcome generator whose cross-arm moments are planning assumptions, not source estimates, temporal ICC, root-mean Dbar covariance, a 576-tuple witness, or empirical effects. The v4a source-structural Dbar correlation matrix is frozen separately as a target constraint that future tuple feasibility must construct or reject with an allowed exact witness; it is not derived from the generic-decision atoms. The decisive fact semantics remain observable exactly once at the registered origin while typed truth and oracle metadata remain hidden from the future SUT. The package publishes no source row, natural-language surface, tape, subject, donor, twin, planning atom, feasibility membership, power replicate, model output, CUDA run, or outcome. Its CLI/read closure cannot prove that the whole machine never held source data, cannot resist an administrator changing code plus tests, does not provide an external anti-grinding witness or WORM timestamp, and validates only ordinary filesystem default streams rather than NTFS alternate data streams. It defines the scope of a future structural inventory but does not authorize materialization until this protocol and artifact have an external publication anchor. It authorizes no current source execution, tuple feasibility, model, development, qualification, formal run, production ACTIVE state, real-human claim, or Appendable/Readable/Learnable/Steerable evidence."
